# Semgrep ignore rules
# See: https://semgrep.dev/docs/ignoring-files-folders-code/

# jsx-not-internationalized: No near-term localization plans for this project.
# All UI strings are intentionally in English only. Suppressing across all frontend files.
frontend/src/

# load-testing: Developer-only tooling run locally against a test environment.
# subprocess.run uses a fully-qualified list (no shell=True, no user-controlled input).
load-testing/

# platform/build: Internal CI build tooling. subprocess.run calls use list form
# with sys.executable and pathlib.Path values — no shell interpolation.
platform/build/

# infra/tools: Operator deployment utilities run locally or in CI, not
# exposed to external input. URLs and paths come from CloudFormation outputs.
# regex_dos in stage_events_gsis.py: pattern matches fixed CloudFormation
# resource ID format, not user-supplied input.
infra/tools/

# services/identity-access/tests: Test fixtures with hardcoded passwords are
# intentional test utilities. Passwords never reach production.
# services/forums/src and services/contributions-scoring/src *_client.py:
# urllib dynamic-url findings are suppressed via .bandit; these internal
# service clients call env-var-configured VPC endpoints, not user-supplied URLs.
# Tracked separately for urllib scheme validation fix.
services/identity-access/tests/conftest.py

# .cfn_nag_suppress.yaml: cfn_nag suppression list — not a Semgrep rule file.
# Semgrep incorrectly parses it as a Semgrep YAML rule and reports missing
# metadata/language/message fields. The file has no Semgrep rules.
.cfn_nag_suppress.yaml

# platform/seed/cfn.py: CloudFormation custom resource response helper.
# The ResponseURL is a pre-signed S3 URL injected by CloudFormation itself —
# not user-supplied input. Already annotated with # noqa: S310 inline.
platform/seed/cfn.py
